  "body": "Integrates the three M2 branches into one consistent PED v2.0 and closes the Architecture, Technology and Initial Design Baseline.\n\n## Requirements traceability\n\nRTM v2.1 resolves the matrix into one document. Merging the three M2 branches had left it carrying its v1.0 sections, the v2.0 columns and a second M2 table side by side.\n\nThe M2 columns are populated from the decisions that now exist: ASR-01 to ASR-05 as the quality drivers, the ADR-001 modules as the architecture responsibilities, the ADR-002 rules and the permission matrix as the data constraints, the ADR-003 stack as the technology decision, and ADR-004 to ADR-006 as the design and interface decisions.\n\nFR-008, NFR-001 and NFR-002 move to In Development against real files and 23 passing tests. Fourteen requirements read Not yet implemented.\n\nThe FR-008 trace runs from the scenario through to verification. The FR-003 trace sits beside it and stops at the design step, with the reason it was sequenced second.\n\n## Baseline\n\nBL-002 is accepted with conditions. The Appendix D fields are completed against the artefacts in the repository, the contents table links every item to its evidence, and four decisions are held outside the baseline with an owner and a trigger each.\n\nBL-002 also records what it does not claim. Three requirements are in development, fourteen are not started, and the backend stores requests in memory, supplies the caller identity rather than authenticating it, and records no history event.\n\n## Registers\n\nThe Risk Register is reviewed against the new evidence. RSK-014 and RSK-018 drop, because ADR-003 records its alternatives and ADR-004 rejected the State pattern on proportionality. RSK-017 rises, because five direct dependencies and a lock file now exist and nothing audits them. RSK-011 and RSK-019 are recorded as materialised. RSK-022 is new and covers the risk of reading 23 tests on an in-memory slice as evidence for NFR-001 to NFR-003.\n\nDEP-001 to DEP-004 close. The permission matrix exists, the stack is selected, and the Assignment 2 sections behind ADR-001 and ADR-002 are named.\n\nThe Decision Log gains DEC-012 for the automated checks and DEC-013 for dependency tracking. The ADR index points at six recorded decisions.\n\nThe AI Usage Register is completed across all four rows with the tool, the contribution, the verification applied and what changed as a result.\n\n## Repository and documentation\n\nThe 1965 installed package files under `app/backend/node_modules` are removed from tracking under DEC-013. The manifest and lock file stay, so `npm ci` rebuilds the tree exactly.\n\nThe technology baseline table now matches the versions that run, taken from the lock file and the workflow. ADR-003 carries the Render source behind its staging claim, the technology selection cites the Assignment 2 section behind the persistence constraint, and Assignment 2 is registered as SRC-A2.\n\nThe API v1 contract is completed from the implemented endpoint: path and body parameters, the conditional fields P-02 requires, the success shape, all five error responses, and the three limitations that hold FR-008 at In Development.\n\nGovernance controls are rechecked at the gate rather than relying on the 9 September readback. The project README carries the current state, prerequisites and run instructions.\n\n## Files owned by other members\n\nThis branch edits files Dewald and Liam own. That is integration work under the same arrangement as the M1 citations pass, and each commit message says what changed and why. The engineering reasoning in ADR-001 to ADR-006 is untouched.\n\n## Checks\n\n23 tests pass under `npm test` and `npx tsc --noEmit` passes, both through `.github/workflows/ci.yml`. Every internal link in the repository resolves. No file under `node_modules` is tracked.\n",
